  "native-adaptation": {
    "execution": "FreeRTOS CPU parses bounded AnnexB SPS/PPS and IDR+P headers, plans retained reference slots and registers; VE executes CAVLC, intra/inter prediction, inverse transforms, deblocking and writeback.",
    "parser_source": "h264_nalu.c:H264DecodeSps,H264DecodePps,H264DecodeSliceHeader",
    "parser_adaptation": "Restricted syntax/field order with bounded software bit reads replacing CedarC GetBits callbacks; no CedarC runtime library linked.",
    "register_source": "cedrus_h264.c:cedrus_set_params,cedrus_write_frame_list,_cedrus_write_ref_list,cedrus_skip_bits; CedarC H264ConfigureRefFrameRegister/H264ConfigureRefListRegister and A733 instructions corroborate field positions.",
    "license": "CedarC GNU LGPL version2 notices retained in adaptation; Cedrus GPL-2.0-or-later.",
    "lifetime": "Fixed VGA input and two reference/output/MV slots with persistent context scratch. Cedrus successful job completion supports healthy input refill; CedarC sliding-window marking retires the previous reference after its consumer completes. Private copied-output ACK ownership is separate. No fault reuse, unmapping, reclamation or physical drain qualification.",
    "fullhd": "Same parser/controller/application; coded 1920x1088 with canonical bottom crop to 1920x1080. Cedrus internal SRAM width branch and effective A733 H264MallocFrmBuffer corroborate external-scratch choice; CedarC field MV formula corroborated by pinned A733 instructions. Existing extended WB/NC providers, fixed reference pool, immutable retained CPU ledger and bounded visible-row copying."
  },
